{"title": "Show HN: A malleable and formally verified Web engine", "link": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50285197", "summary": "<p>Hello HN,<p>I've been working on a new Web engine, build around two ideas:<p>- use formal methods from day one.\n- make it modular.<p>The modularity is orientated towards the following goals:<p>- enabling shipping anywhere, including on IOS in the EU as per Apple’s guidelines.\n- only write code for stuff the OS or application platform cannot do for you: keep binary size to a minimum and achieve native performance.\n- developer choice: bring what you want, and only build what you need.<p>For example you can choose a JS engine like v8 or Boa, or just bring your own. The entire graphics pipeline consists of components whose implementation can be swapped-out, with currently a relatively fast path on Mac integrating with Core Animation and a slower cross platform path.<p>Project is at <a href=\"https://github.com/gterzian/formal-web\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/gterzian/formal-web</a><p>Intro essay at: <a href=\"https://medium.com/@polyglot_factotum/how-i-am-building-a-web-engine-181c0b1faadd\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://medium.com/@polyglot_factotum/how-i-am-building-a-we...</a><p>Please let me know what you think.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50285197\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50285197</a></p>\n<p>Points: 3</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>", "published": "2026-10-29T06:28:03+00:00", "source": "Hacker News Best", "category": "techblog", "matched_entities": {}, "ontology": {"repo": "BlogRadar", "category": "techblog", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "source_event_model": "blog_post", "event_model_id": "tech.blog_post", "evidence_policy_ids": ["source_metadata", "article_text"], "event_model_payload": {"headline": "Show HN: A malleable and formally verified Web engine", "source_name": "Hacker News Best", "source_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50285197", "published_at": "2026-10-29T06:28:03+00:00", "summary": "<p>Hello HN,<p>I've been working on a new Web engine, build around two ideas:<p>- use formal methods from day one.\n- make it modular.<p>The modularity is orientated towards the following goals:<p>- enabling shipping anywhere, including on IOS in the EU as per Apple’s guidelines.\n- only write code for stuff the OS or application platform cannot do for you: keep binary size to a minimum and achieve native performance.\n- developer choice: bring what you want, and only build what you need.<p>For example you can choose a JS engine like v8 or Boa, or just bring your own. The entire graphics pipeline consists of components whose implementation can be swapped-out, with currently a relatively fast path on Mac integrating with Core Animation and a slower cross platform path.<p>Project is at <a href=\"https://github.com/gterzian/formal-web\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/gterzian/formal-web</a><p>Intro essay at: <a href=\"https://medium.com/@polyglot_factotum/how-i-am-building-a-web-engine-181c0b1faadd\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://medium.com/@polyglot_factotum/how-i-am-building-a-we...</a><p>Please let me know what you think.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50285197\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50285197</a></p>\n<p>Points: 3</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>"}}, "logged_at": "2026-10-29T06:47:23.218207+00:00"}
